<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    This project exists for exactly one reason: to actually execute SwissEphNet's
    netstandard2.0 asset. SwissEphNet.csproj multi-targets
    netstandard2.0;net8.0;net10.0, but Tests/SwissEphNet.Tests only targets
    net8.0;net10.0: a modern .NET host always resolves the net8.0/net10.0 asset
    in preference to netstandard2.0 when both are available from a
    ProjectReference, so the netstandard2.0 build has never actually been run by
    anything. That gap let a real bug ship silently: an extension method that
    called itself recursively on netstandard2.0 (no such call ever throws a
    compile error there, since C# happily binds the call to the extension method
    itself when no better match exists) but was masked entirely on net8.0/net10.0,
    where the real BCL instance method exists and wins overload resolution. See
    docs/known-issues.md for the write-up.

    net48 is a deliberate choice of "host that cannot use the net8.0/net10.0
    asset": a .NET Framework consumer resolves a multi-targeted ProjectReference
    down to the highest asset it can actually use, which for a .NET Framework
    TFM is netstandard2.0 (net8.0/net10.0 assets require a modern .NET runtime
    that .NET Framework does not have). That forces exactly the asset this
    project exists to exercise, with no special MSBuild wiring needed beyond
    picking a .NET Framework TFM.

    net462 is the second TFM alongside net48, added for the same reason: it is
    the lowest .NET Framework version that can practically consume the
    netstandard2.0 asset (netstandard2.0 support starts here; earlier .NET
    Framework versions either cannot reference it at all or need patches this
    repo has no reason to assume a consumer applied). net48 alone leaves the
    low end of that range unexercised: a regression that only shows up on
    older .NET Framework runtimes would pass here unnoticed. Both TFMs resolve
    the same netstandard2.0 asset from the ProjectReference below (confirmed
    via project.assets.json: each target's SwissEphNet entry reports
    ".NETStandard,Version=v2.0", not net8.0 or net10.0).

    The v4.6.2 targeting pack is not installed on every machine that builds
    this repo, so the ItemGroup below pulls it from
    Microsoft.NETFramework.ReferenceAssemblies instead of assuming it is
    present locally. It is a build-time-only reference, never a runtime
    dependency of anything this repo ships (SwissEphNet.csproj itself has
    none; see scripts/verify-no-dependencies.ps1).

    This project is intentionally NOT included in SwissEphNet.CrossPlatform.slnf,
    the filter used for Linux/cross-platform builds, since .NET Framework cannot
    build or run outside Windows (same reason Programs/SweWin, a WinForms app, is
    excluded from that filter). It is part of SwissEphNet.sln and runs on Windows
    only, via `dotnet test Tests/NetStandard20Smoke.Tests -c Release`.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net462;net48</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>NetStandard20Smoke.Tests</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>SwissEphNet.NetStandard20Smoke.Tests</RootNamespace>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <GenerateAssemblyConfigurationAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyConfigurationAttribute>
    <GenerateAssemblyCompanyAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyCompanyAttribute>
    <GenerateAssemblyProductAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyProductAttribute>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\SwissEphNet\SwissEphNet.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" />
    <!--
      Matches Tests/SwissEphNet.Tests: stays on xunit v2, not the v3 used by
      Tools/BaselineVerify.Tests, so its runner needs the matching v2 major.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" VersionOverride="2.8.2">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" />
    <!--
      Supplies the net462 reference assemblies without requiring that
      targeting pack to be installed on the build machine (it is not, on
      every machine this repo builds on). Test-only and build-time-only:
      PrivateAssets="all" keeps it out of this project's own dependency
      surface, and it never touches SwissEphNet.csproj, the project
      scripts/verify-no-dependencies.ps1 actually gates.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NETFramework.ReferenceAssemblies" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
